            "horizon_end_utc": "2026-11-13T08:00:00Z",
            "invalidation_reason": "below 158.04 the pair is back under the pre-release shelf and the 158.061 dossier capture, which means the CPI repricing failed for this pair.",
            "invalidation_text": "any trade below 158.04; the thesis is also broken by an M15 close below 158.20 while US500 is down more than 1% on the day, a Japanese official verbal warning, or the US 2y giving back most of its CPI-day rise.",
            "main_alternative": {
              "market_move": "a haven-yen bid on an equity selloff, or seven-week range supply at 158.77-159.04, sends USDJPY back below 158.04 toward the 9 Nov low 157.670.",
              "probability_pct": 30.0
            },
            "mechanism": "the hot October core CPI (+0.296% vs 0.2% consensus, BLS) reprices the US front end (2y +15-17 bp, context) while the JGB 2y had already fallen from 1.891% (4 Nov) to 1.732% (6 Nov) with US2Y at 4.51%; USDJPY's 20-day correlation to US10Y changes is +0.62 (beta 0.038 per point, US500 beta only 0.10), and yen speculators net long 27% of open interest must cover above 158.770.",
            "missing_fields": [],
            "opposite_mechanism": "a haven-yen bid if the rates shock knocks equities (5 Nov: USDJPY -0.55% with US500 -4.86%) and range-top supply at 158.40-159.04; each predicts a return under 158.39 inside the horizon.",
            "positioning": "CFTC JPY speculators net long yen 102,321 of 380,641 (27%, COT 3 Nov) are forced to cover above 158.770; sellers have capped 158.40-159.04 on every D1 test since 24 Sep (highs 158.404, 159.037, 158.455, 158.512, 158.754, 158.952, 158.603, 158.605, 158.770, 158.669, 158.585; no D1 close above 158.84); official-action risk near 159.75-160.40, where the 1-2 Sep up-leg reversed. Crowd trade: long yen, wrong while USDJPY holds above 158.39.",
            "priced": "prior_pricing AMBIGUOUS; 5-day -0.65 ATR to the 9 Nov close (158.471 to 157.988), so nothing hawkish was priced before the print; the 158.630 capture sits +1.08 ATR over the 20-day mean 157.822, +1.43 over the 50-day 157.562 and -0.61 under the 200-day 159.086; 20-day range 156.075-158.770, 14 pips under its top; ATR percentile 30; the 48 h to 15 min drift and the implied move are not observed.",
